Z||000000||BN Boomer||05-20-2000||09:58 PM||||While I was on my way up to the Sultan Basin for a little target shooting and traveling eastbound on US 2, just west of Sultan, I passed 5 Fieros traveling westbound. I figure the chances of seeing 5 consecutive Fieros is about the same odds as the time I saw 6 DeLoreans cruising around Ocean Shores, must've been some sort of club or group outing. The first one was a silver GT fastback, and I was paying so much attention to it, assuming it to be alone, that I didn't really notice much about the next 4, except that there were indeed 5 altogether with one being red and another being yellow. Then, on the way home, I saw a white GT fastback leaving the town of Snohomish, my home, with the license plate "PROUD 1". Anyone from here?||||reg||6
